<title>GREECE: ATHLETICS-BOLDON SETS YEAR'S FASTEST 100 METRES TIME.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-BOLDON SETS YEAR'S FASTEST 100 METRES TIME.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trinidad's Ato Boldon set a year's best of 9.87 seconds in the second round of the men's 100 metres on the opening day of the world championships on Saturday.</p>
<p>Only four men have ever run faster.</p>
<p>Boldon's training partner Maurice Greene, the American champion, was second in 9.90.</p>
